<title>USA: Teva Pharmaceutical consolidates shares.</title>
<headline>Teva Pharmaceutical consolidates shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd, Israel's largest pharmaceutical firm, said Monday its shareholders approved a 10-for-one consolidation of its shares.</p>
<p>Teva said the consolidation was approved by shareholders at an extraordinary meeting in Israel.</p>
<p>It said the consolidation will result in each American Depositary Share being the equivalent of one newly consolidated ordinary share instead of 10 ordinary shares.</p>
<p>Since ADRs currently represent ten old ordinary shares, the consolidation will not change the economic value of an ADR or the legal rights associated with an ADR, it said.</p>
</text>
